\textbf{Input shift} ($K{=}1$): the CRM receives an arbitrary single sample rather than the argmin-centered input it was trained on, causing correction to fall below baseline (10.3\% vs.\ 11.6\%).
\textbf{Task shift} (leave-task-out): training the CRM on 15 tasks and evaluating on 5 held-out tasks yields 2\% vs.\ 14\% VLA-only; the CRM actively degrades on unseen tasks, confirming that corrections are task-specific and require representative calibration data~\cite{angelopoulos2023gentle}. All results in Table~\ref{tab:main} are in-distribution.
